    "explanation": "To the rider: your core claim — that this trip was driven well off the direct route — is upheld on the evidence. The governing GPS trace (EV-GPS-00106) measures 10.78 km against the booked optimal of 7.2 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00106), an excess of 3.58 km (49.72%). That clears POL-RD-01's establishment gate (excess over 20% of optimal AND over 0.8 km absolute), so a deviation is established. Under POL-RD-02, the fare being metered (EV-FARE-00106), the recomputed optimal-route fare is (3.80 + 0.75 x 7.2 + 0.28 x 19.0) x 1.0 surge + 0.80 platform fee + 0 on-route ERP = 15.32. Charged total was 26.04, so the refund is 26.04 - 15.32 = 10.72, rounded up to SGD 10.75. The $5.50 of ERP you highlighted is the two CTE gantries (3.00 at Braddell Rd + 2.50 at Chin Swee Rd tunnel), both off the optimal route; under POL-RD-09(1) that ERP is already comprehended in the 10.75 refund and is itemised for transparency only — it is not added again on top. Your request for the full $26.04 is not granted: the excess falls just below the 50%-of-optimal / 8.0 km materiality line (the trace figure governs, not the rounded 10.8 km convenience copy on the fare record), and 10.75 is far below the 90%-of-charged figure that would trigger a FULL_REFUND, so a PARTIAL_REFUND is the correct outcome. To the driver: the deviation is established but not material, so no POL-RD-06 driver-profile pattern test is engaged and no driver-conduct referral follows; in any event the profile shows 0 deviation flags across 96 trips. The trace was not impaired for policy purposes (169 fixes, 10-second interval, no gaps, max gap 0 s), so no corroboration requirement or escalation arises. No exculpatory clause applies: no traffic advisory evidenced anything (the sole advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-00106-01 carries no payload), the single chat message is a rider complaint rather than a detour instruction and has a null waypoint_hint, and no pickup or dropoff was amended. Both charged gantries are matched to the trace well within 250 m, so no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity correction is due on top; and the billed distance (10.8 km) is not below the trace (10.78 km), so no driver compensation is payable under POL-RD-04. The amount the ruling moves is a refund to the filing rider of SGD 10.75; the charge otherwise stands.",
