    "explanation": "Both sides' advocates largely agree, and so do I. Measuring the deviation the way POL-RD-01 requires, on the governing GPS trace (EV-GPS-00106, 10.78 km) against the booked optimal (EV-TRIP-00106, 7.2 km), the excess is 3.58 km — 49.72% of optimal. That clears the establishment gate (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%, both tests pass), but it sits just below the 50% / 8.0 km line that would make the deviation MATERIAL. The trip_record's rounded 10.8 km may not be used for this test, and using it would only have produced the same non-material answer. Because the deviation is established but not material, the POL-RD-06 driver-profile uplift and conduct referral are not engaged — and in any event driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across 96 completed trips, so no repeat pattern exists.\n\nThe fare was METERED, so POL-RD-02 runs. Charged total: 26.04. Recomputed optimal-route fare: (3.80 base + 0.75 x 7.2 + 0.28 x 19.0) x 1.0 surge + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP on the optimal route + 0 fixed surcharge + 0 waiting fee = 15.32. Refund: 26.04 - 15.32 = 10.72, rounded up to SGD 10.75. That is 41.2% of charged_total — below the 90% needed for a full refund — and above the 0.50 de minimis floor. Ruling: PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 10.75 to the rider.\n\nThe $5.50 of ERP you highlighted is already comprehended in that 10.75, because the recomputed fare credits only gantries lying on the optimal route and the optimal Thomson Road route carries none. It is itemised for transparency and is NOT added on top (POL-RD-09(1)) — your total exposure is the single 10.75 figure, not 16.25. Both charged CTE gantries are matched to the trace (nearest fixes 0.0 m and 24.1 m, inside the 250 m crossing radius) and there is no airport surcharge, so there is no billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4).\n\nThe trace is not impaired: 169 fixes, 100% coverage, 10-second sampling, zero gaps — nowhere near the POL-RD-07 limbs — so the deviation stands on the trace and needs no independent corroboration. Nothing exonerates the excess. The only traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00106-01) carries no payload, so POL-RD-03 cannot run and no closure is excused. The single chat message (08:46:30, 'why we at havelock?') is your own complaint, not an instruction, its waypoint_hint is null and no road is named, so POL-RD-04 does not apply and no distance is excluded. There is no unbilled-distance shortfall (billed 10.8 km against a 10.78 km trace), so no driver compensation is due under POL-RD-04. Finally, no POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: trip identifiers match across all three artifacts, the trace is complete, no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact, and 10.75 is far below the 150.00 ceiling."
